        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bulawayo Railway Museum, Cape Colony, South Africa\n- People: Cecil John Rhodes\n- Topics: railway exhibits, political roles\n\nFacts:\n- In 1890, Cecil John Rhodes became Prime Minister of the Cape Colony.\n- Cecil John Rhodes served as Prime Minister of the Cape Colony until 1896.\n- In 1897, the oldest exhibits at the Bulawayo Railway Museum date back to that year.\n- The Bulawayo Railway Museum includes Cecil Rhodes' personal railway coach among its oldest exhibits.\n- Cecil John Rhodes was born on 5 July 1853 and died on 26 March 1902.\n- Cecil John Rhodes was a British businessman, mining magnate, and politician in South Africa.",
